  "slug": "spatial-transcriptomics-6c8f",
  "summary": "Matched serum proteomics and N-glycoproteomics, plus glycan–phosphorylation co-variation across 1,211 tumor proteomes, make cross-layer tumor states testable.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across these preprints is the integration of multiple molecular layers to resolve tumor regulatory states. Matched serum proteomics and intact N-glycoproteomics from 100 participants, analysed with a new differential-trend-subtype (DTS) framework, link glycan remodelling to ovarian cancer. In pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma, spatial transcriptomics of CA19-9-positive regions yields four transcriptional programs associated with patient survival and cell-line drug sensitivity. PTMlink extends this logic to post-translational regulation by scoring glycosylation–phosphorylation co-variation across 1,211 tumor proteomes. What is new is the testability of cross-layer relationships, in which co-variation and molecular signatures are quantified directly rather than inferred from single modalities. The remaining items, a machine learning analysis of long COVID transcriptomes and an integrated breast and ovarian gene-expression screen, apply similar integrative logic in more exploratory, hypothesis-generating settings.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
